#: ../../source/sax_README.md:1
msgid "sax js"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:3
msgid "A sax-style parser for XML and HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:5
msgid ""
"Designed with [node](http://nodejs.org/) in mind, but should work fine in"
" the browser or other CommonJS implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:8
msgid "What This Is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:10
msgid "A very simple tool to parse through an XML string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:11
msgid "A stepping stone to a streaming HTML parser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:12
msgid ""
"A handy way to deal with RSS and other mostly-ok-but-kinda-broken XML "
"docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:15
msgid "What This Is (probably) Not"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:17
msgid "An HTML Parser - That's a fine goal, but this isn't it.  It's just XML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:19
msgid ""
"A DOM Builder - You can use it to build an object model out of XML, but "
"it doesn't do that out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:21
msgid "XSLT - No DOM = no querying."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:22
msgid ""
"100% Compliant with (some other SAX implementation) - Most SAX "
"implementations are in Java and do a lot more than this does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:24
msgid ""
"An XML Validator - It does a little validation when in strict mode, but "
"not much."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:26
msgid ""
"A Schema-Aware XSD Thing - Schemas are an exercise in fetishistic "
"masochism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:28
msgid "A DTD-aware Thing - Fetching DTDs is a much bigger job."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:30
msgid "Regarding `<!DOCTYPE`s and `<!ENTITY`s"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:32
msgid ""
"The parser will handle the basic XML entities in text nodes and attribute"
" values: `&amp; &lt; &gt; &apos; &quot;`. It's possible to define "
"additional entities in XML by putting them in the DTD. This parser "
"doesn't do anything with that. If you want to listen to the `ondoctype` "
"event, and then fetch the doctypes, and read the entities and add them to"
" `parser.ENTITIES`, then be my guest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:39
msgid ""
"Unknown entities will fail in strict mode, and in loose mode, will pass "
"through unmolested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:42
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:89
msgid "Arguments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:91
msgid "Pass the following arguments to the parser function.  All are optional."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:93
msgid "`strict` - Boolean. Whether or not to be a jerk. Default: `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:95
msgid ""
"`opt` - Object bag of settings regarding string formatting.  All default "
"to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:97
msgid "Settings supported:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:99
msgid "`trim` - Boolean. Whether or not to trim text and comment nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:100
msgid ""
"`normalize` - Boolean. If true, then turn any whitespace into a single "
"space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:102
msgid ""
"`lowercase` - Boolean. If true, then lowercase tag names and attribute "
"names in loose mode, rather than uppercasing them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:104
msgid "`xmlns` - Boolean. If true, then namespaces are supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:105
msgid "`position` - Boolean. If false, then don't track line/col/position."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:106
msgid ""
"`strictEntities` - Boolean. If true, only parse [predefined XML "
"entities](http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-xml/#sec-predefined-ent) (`&amp;`, "
"`&apos;`, `&gt;`, `&lt;`, and `&quot;`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:110
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:112
msgid ""
"`write` - Write bytes onto the stream. You don't have to do this all at "
"once. You can keep writing as much as you want."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:115
msgid ""
"`close` - Close the stream. Once closed, no more data may be written "
"until it is done processing the buffer, which is signaled by the `end` "
"event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:118
msgid ""
"`resume` - To gracefully handle errors, assign a listener to the `error` "
"event. Then, when the error is taken care of, you can call `resume` to "
"continue parsing. Otherwise, the parser will not continue while in an "
"error state."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:123
msgid "Members"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:125
msgid "At all times, the parser object will have the following members:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:127
msgid ""
"`line`, `column`, `position` - Indications of the position in the XML "
"document where the parser currently is looking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:130
msgid "`startTagPosition` - Indicates the position where the current tag starts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:132
msgid ""
"`closed` - Boolean indicating whether or not the parser can be written "
"to. If it's `true`, then wait for the `ready` event to write again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:135
msgid "`strict` - Boolean indicating whether or not the parser is a jerk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:137
msgid "`opt` - Any options passed into the constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:139
msgid "`tag` - The current tag being dealt with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:141
msgid "And a bunch of other stuff that you probably shouldn't touch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:143
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:145
msgid ""
"All events emit with a single argument. To listen to an event, assign a "
"function to `on<eventname>`. Functions get executed in the this-context "
"of the parser object. The list of supported events are also in the "
"exported `EVENTS` array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:150
msgid ""
"When using the stream interface, assign handlers using the EventEmitter "
"`on` function in the normal fashion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:153
msgid ""
"`error` - Indication that something bad happened. The error will be "
"hanging out on `parser.error`, and must be deleted before parsing can "
"continue. By listening to this event, you can keep an eye on that kind of"
" stuff. Note: this happens *much* more in strict mode. Argument: instance"
" of `Error`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:158
msgid "`text` - Text node. Argument: string of text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:160
msgid "`doctype` - The `<!DOCTYPE` declaration. Argument: doctype string."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:162
msgid ""
"`processinginstruction` - Stuff like `<?xml foo=\"blerg\" ?>`. Argument: "
"object with `name` and `body` members. Attributes are not parsed, as "
"processing instructions have implementation dependent semantics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:166
msgid ""
"`sgmldeclaration` - Random SGML declarations. Stuff like `<!ENTITY p>` "
"would trigger this kind of event. This is a weird thing to support, so it"
" might go away at some point. SAX isn't intended to be used to parse "
"SGML, after all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:171
msgid ""
"`opentagstart` - Emitted immediately when the tag name is available, but "
"before any attributes are encountered.  Argument: object with a `name` "
"field and an empty `attributes` set.  Note that this is the same object "
"that will later be emitted in the `opentag` event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:176
msgid ""
"`opentag` - An opening tag. Argument: object with `name` and "
"`attributes`. In non-strict mode, tag names are uppercased, unless the "
"`lowercase` option is set.  If the `xmlns` option is set, then it will "
"contain namespace binding information on the `ns` member, and will have a"
" `local`, `prefix`, and `uri` member."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:182
msgid ""
"`closetag` - A closing tag. In loose mode, tags are auto-closed if their "
"parent closes. In strict mode, well-formedness is enforced. Note that "
"self-closing tags will have `closeTag` emitted immediately after "
"`openTag`. Argument: tag name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:187
msgid ""
"`attribute` - An attribute node.  Argument: object with `name` and "
"`value`. In non-strict mode, attribute names are uppercased, unless the "
"`lowercase` option is set.  If the `xmlns` option is set, it will also "
"contains namespace information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:192
msgid "`comment` - A comment node.  Argument: the string of the comment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:194
msgid "`opencdata` - The opening tag of a `<![CDATA[` block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:196
msgid ""
"`cdata` - The text of a `<![CDATA[` block. Since `<![CDATA[` blocks can "
"get quite large, this event may fire multiple times for a single block, "
"if it is broken up into multiple `write()`s. Argument: the string of "
"random character data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:201
msgid "`closecdata` - The closing tag (`]]>`) of a `<![CDATA[` block."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:203
msgid ""
"`opennamespace` - If the `xmlns` option is set, then this event will "
"signal the start of a new namespace binding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:206
msgid ""
"`closenamespace` - If the `xmlns` option is set, then this event will "
"signal the end of a namespace binding."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:209
msgid "`end` - Indication that the closed stream has ended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:211
msgid ""
"`ready` - Indication that the stream has reset, and is ready to be "
"written to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:214
msgid ""
"`noscript` - In non-strict mode, `<script>` tags trigger a `\"script\"` "
"event, and their contents are not checked for special xml characters. If "
"you pass `noscript: true`, then this behavior is suppressed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:218
msgid "Reporting Problems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/sax_README.md:220
msgid ""
"It's best to write a failing test if you find an issue.  I will always "
"accept pull requests with failing tests if they demonstrate intended "
"behavior, but it is very hard to figure out what issue you're describing "
"without a test.  Writing a test is also the best way for you yourself to "
"figure out if you really understand the issue you think you have with "
"sax-js."
msgstr ""

